### Security Operations Fundamentals and Guidance
* **Presentation**: Michael Peck presented [Security Operations Fundamentals and Guidance](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-saag-security-operations-fundamentals-and-guidance-00) (`draft-opsawg-ops-guidance`).
* **Technical Overview**:
  * Provides non-mandatory guidance for protocol designers to consider Security Operations Center (SOC) capabilities, threat intelligence, security monitoring, and incident response requirements.
  * Differentiates Network Operations Centers (NOCs, focused on network stability) from SOCs (focused on security and resilience).
  * Addresses privacy considerations: while security monitoring requires operational visibility, it must be balanced against user privacy and pervasive monitoring concerns (RFC 7258).
* **Discussion**:
  * Eric Rescorla and Dennis Jackson noted in chat that on-path inspection or dissectors used for security monitoring present identical network vantage points to passive pervasive monitoring or on-path attackers, requiring explicit privacy analysis under RFC 7258. Michael Peck agreed to refine the privacy considerations text in future revisions.

